<title>HUNGARY: Hungary 1996 maize crop up 29 pct at 5.9 mln T.</title>
<headline>Hungary 1996 maize crop up 29 pct at 5.9 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary 1996 maize crop was 5.9 million tonnes, 29 percent more than in 1995, the Central Statistical Office (KSH) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The crop was planted on 1.05 million hectares, up two percent from 1995, with a yield of 5.6 tonnes per hectare.</p>
<p>The sunflower seed harvest was 866,000 tonnes in 1996, against 777,000 tonnes in 1995 despite a 17,000-hectare decline in the sowing area to 474,000 hectares, KSH said.</p>
<p>The sugarbeet crop was 4.7 million tonnes last year, up 12 percent from 1995, it added.</p>
<p>KSH reported in September that Hungary's 1995-96 grain crop excluding maize was 5.31 million tonnes, of which wheat was 3.92 million tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
